parts":[{"text":"உடைத்து","lemma":"uṭaittu","gloss":"it has"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"clitic of question"}],"gloss":"does it have?"},{"surface":"தோழி","parts":[{"text":"தோழி","lemma":"tōḻi","gloss":"friend"}],"gloss":"O friend!"},{"surface":"நீடுமயிர்","parts":[{"text":"நீடு","lemma":"nīṭu","gloss":"long"},{"text":"மயிர்","lemma":"mayir","gloss":"hair"}],"gloss":"long-haired"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கடும்பல்","parts":[{"text":"கடும்பல்","lemma":"கடும்பல்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஊகக்","parts":[{"text":"ஊகக்","lemma":"ஊகக்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கறைவிரல்","parts":[{"text":"கறைவிரல்","lemma":"கறைவிரல்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஏற்றை","parts":[{"text":"ஏற்றை","lemma":"ஏற்றை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"புடைத்து","parts":[{"text":"புடை","lemma":"puṭai","gloss":"to strike"},{"text":"து","lemma":"tu","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having struck"},{"surface":"ஒடு","parts":[{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"oṭu","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with"},{"surface":"புடைஇ","parts":[{"text":"புடை","lemma":"puṭai","gloss":"to break open"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having broken open"},{"surface":"பூநாறு","parts":[{"text":"பூ","lemma":"pū","gloss":"flower"},{"text":"நாறு","lemma":"nāṟu","gloss":"to smell"}],"gloss":"flower-scented"},{"surface":"பலவுக்கனி","parts":[{"text":"பலவு","lemma":"palavu","gloss":"jackfruit tree"},{"text":"கனி","lemma":"kaṉi","gloss":"ripe fruit"}],"gloss":"ripe jackfruit"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"காந்தள்","parts":[{"text":"காந்தள்","lemma":"kāntal","gloss":"Malabar glory lily"}],"gloss":"glory lily"},{"surface":"அம்","parts":[{"text":"அம்","lemma":"am","gloss":"beautiful"}],"gloss":"beautiful"},{"surface":"சிறுகுடி","parts":[{"text":"சிறுமை","lemma":"ciṟumai","gloss":"small"},{"text":"குடி","lemma":"kuṭi","gloss":"hamlet"}],"gloss":"small hamlet"},{"surface":"கமழும்","parts":[{"text":"கமழ்","lemma":"kamaḻ","gloss":"to be fragrant"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"fragrant"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஓங்குமலை","parts":[{"text":"ஓங்கு","lemma":"ōṅku","gloss":"to rise high"},{"text":"மலை","lemma":"malai","gloss":"mountain"}],"gloss":"high mountain"},{"surface":"நாடனொடு","parts":[{"text":"நாடன்","lemma":"nāṭaṉ","gloss":"lord of the land"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"oṭu","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with the lord of the land"},{"surface":"அமைந்த","parts":[{"text":"அமைந்த","lemma":"அமைந்த","gloss":"established"}],"gloss":"established","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நம்","parts":[{"text":"நம்","lemma":"nam","gloss":"our"}],"gloss":"our"},{"surface":"தொடர்பே","parts":[{"text":"தொடர்பு","lemma":"toṭarpu","gloss":"connection/bond"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"bond indeed"}]}],"literal":"Even if the earth shifts, even if water and fire clash / Even if a boundary appears to the glistening-waved great sea / Fearing the gossip of cruel-mouthed women / What harm does it have, O friend? The long-haired / Sharp-toothed, black-fingered male langur / Striking and breaking open the flower-scented ripe jackfruit / Which makes the small hamlet of beautiful glory lilies fragrant / Our bond established with the lord of the high mountain!","translation":"Even if the earth shifts, even if water and fire clash, or a boundary appears to the great sea of glistening waves, what harm can come to our bond, O friend, established with the lord of the high mountain? In his land, a long-haired, sharp-toothed, black-fingered male langur beats and breaks open the flower-scented ripe jackfruit, filling the small hamlet of beautiful glory lilies with its sweet fragrance.","modern":"தோழியே! பூமி தன் நிலையிலிருந்து பெயர்ந்தாலும், நீரும் நெருப்பும் தம் இயல்பிலிருந்து மாறினாலும், விளங்கும் அலைகளை உடைய பெரிய கடலுக்கு ஒரு எல்லை தோன்றினாலும், கொடிய சொற்களைப் பேசும் பெண்களின் அலர் தூற்றுதலுக்கு அஞ்சி, உயர்ந்த மலைநாட்டோடு நமக்கு உண்டான நட்பு என்ன கேட்டை அடைந்துவிடும்? அந்த மலைநாட்டில், நீண்ட மயிரையும், கூர்மையான பற்களையும், கரிய விரல்களையும் உடைய ஆண் குரங்கு, பூவின் மணம் வீசும் பலாப்பழத்தை அடித்து உடைத்து உண்ணும். அதனால் ஏற்படும் நறுமணம், காந்தள் மலர்கள் நிறைந்த சிறிய குடியிருப்பு முழுவதும் கமழும்.","explanation":"The foster-mother and the villagers have started gossiping about the heroine's secret love affair with the hero. The heroine is deeply worried, but her close friend consoles her, reassuring her of the strength of their love. The friend asserts that even if cosmic catastrophes occur—the earth moving, fire and water reversing their natures, or the boundless ocean finding a limit—their love will never fail or suffer harm. The poem is set in the Kuriñci (mountain) landscape. The image of the male langur breaking open the sweet jackfruit, whose fragrance then fills the entire hamlet of glory lilies, is an implicit metaphor (uḷḷuṟai). It suggests that the hero will soon openly marry the heroine, and just as the broken jackfruit fills the village with fragrance, their union will bring joy and sweet reputation to the entire hamlet, dispelling the bitter gossip.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}